# Test: with no ze running, validate queries declared external programs in declare mode (S-3), never starts their run loop, and fails closed when a program cannot declare
#
# Question: when `ze config validate` runs with no ze listening on a config
# that declares an external plugin and holds a section under that plugin's
# root, does it query the program in declare mode (`ZE_PLUGIN_MODE=declare`,
# never starting its run loop), validate the section against its declared YANG
# schema, report the queried plugin, still accept a config with no section or a
# compiled-in plugin, and fail closed naming the endpoint, `run` line, cause,
# and `ze show plugin conformance run` when a declared program cannot be found?
# Why not a unit test: TestValidateRefusesSectionOfExternalPluginWithoutStartingIt
# proves runValidation over a test helper. This proves the `ze` binary an
# operator runs: the real query-mode invocation, the printed stdout/fix lines,
# and that the run-loop marker is never written.
#
# The declared program honors `ZE_PLUGIN_MODE=declare` by writing a declare-mode
# marker and its Stage 1 declaration line and exiting 0, and writes a run-loop
# marker only if started outside declare mode. Under S-3
# (plan/release/fixes/spec-explicit-plugin-and-attach-config.md, AC-18 / S16),
# Thomas reversed the earlier ruling that offline validation starts no external
# program: offline validation queries external programs in declare mode and
# never starts their run loop.
#
# ze.ssh.port points the ask at the runner's $PORT, where nothing listens, so
# another session's daemon on the default port cannot answer it.
#
# VALIDATES: S-3 / AC-18 / S16 of spec-explicit-plugin-and-attach-config.md
#   beside AC-2 and AC-15 of spec-plugin-external-yang-at-startup.
# PREVENTS: offline validate refusing a valid declare-mode external plugin;
#   starting an external plugin's run loop offline; silently accepting a config
#   whose external plugin binary is missing.
#
# The program is a script the run string hands to a shell by name, because a
# declaration holds double quotes and the config's run string is itself
# double-quoted. It carries no interpreter line and no command of this file
# starts a shell directly: TestNoPythonLeRemains (internal/le/contract_test.go)
# refuses a functional test that embeds either.

option=env:var=ze.ssh.port:value=$PORT

# Honors ZE_PLUGIN_MODE=declare by writing a declare marker and printing its
# Stage 1 declaration line; writes a run-loop marker only outside declare mode.
tmpfs=marker.run:terminator=EOF_RUN
if [ "$ZE_PLUGIN_MODE" = "declare" ]; then
	echo declared > "declared-$1.marker"
	printf '%s\n' '#1 ze-plugin-engine:declare-registration {"protocol-version":1,"wants-config":["acme-shell"],"schemas":[{"module":"acme-shell-conf","namespace":"urn:acme:shell:conf","yang-text":"module acme-shell-conf { namespace \"urn:acme:shell:conf\"; prefix shell; container acme-shell { presence \"The acme shell plugin is configured\"; leaf greeting { type string { length \"1..64\"; } } } }"}]}'
	exit 0
fi
echo started > "started-$1.marker"
EOF_RUN

tmpfs=ze.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
bus {
	endpoint acme-shell {
		external {
			run "sh marker.run by-ze";
		}
		encoding json;
	}
}

acme-shell {
	greeting hello
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=no-section.conf:terminator=EOF_NO_SECTION
bus {
	endpoint acme-shell {
		external {
			run "sh marker.run by-ze";
		}
		encoding json;
	}
}
EOF_NO_SECTION

tmpfs=built-in.conf:terminator=EOF_BUILT_IN
bus {
	endpoint static {
		internal static;
	}
}
EOF_BUILT_IN

tmpfs=missing.conf:terminator=EOF_MISSING
bus {
	endpoint acme-missing {
		external {
			run "/no/such/ze-plugin";
		}
		encoding json;
	}
}
EOF_MISSING

# With no ze running, validate queries acme-shell in declare mode (S-3), joins
# its YANG module, validates the acme-shell section, and names the queried
# plugin without starting its run loop.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate ze.conf:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid: ze.conf
expect=stdout:contains=queried external plugins: acme-shell
reject=stdout:contains=unknown top-level keyword

# A config that declares the plugin and holds no section of it is valid too.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate no-section.conf:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid: no-section.conf
expect=stdout:contains=queried external plugins: acme-shell
reject=stdout:contains=unknown top-level keyword

# A compiled-in plugin is judged with the schema in the binary, with no query.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze config validate built-in.conf:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid: built-in.conf
reject=stdout:contains=queried external plugins:

# Negative: a missing external program fails closed, naming the endpoint, its
# run line, the cause, and the conformance command.
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze config validate missing.conf:exit=1
expect=stdout:contains=configuration invalid: missing.conf
expect=stdout:contains=bus endpoint "acme-missing" (run "/no/such/ze-plugin"): declaration query failed: command not found (exit status 127)
expect=stdout:contains=fix: ze show plugin conformance run "/no/such/ze-plugin"

# Control: the conformance checker runs the same program in declare mode.
cmd=foreground:seq=5:exec=ze show plugin conformance run "sh marker.run by-checker" name acme-shell:exit=0
expect=stdout:pattern=program-starts +declare +pass

expect=file:path=declared-by-ze.marker:exists=true
expect=file:path=declared-by-checker.marker:exists=true
expect=file:path=started-by-ze.marker:absent=true
expect=file:path=started-by-checker.marker:absent=true
